data.content:
Since `TimestampFormatter` is a **static class**, you can't use constructor injection directly. You have two main options:

### Option 1 — Make it non-static (recommended)
Convert to an instance class so it can receive `TimeProvider` via DI:

```csharp
public class TimestampFormatter(TimeProvider timeProvider)
{
    public string Now() => timeProvider.GetUtcNow().ToString("O");
}
```

Register it in DI alongside `TimeProvider`. This is the idiomatic approach.

### Option 2 — Keep it static, pass `TimeProvider` as a parameter
```csharp
public static class TimestampFormatter
{
    public static string Now(TimeProvider timeProvider) =>
        timeProvider.GetUtcNow().ToString("O");
}
```

Simpler change, but every caller must supply the provider.

---

